.Dd February 28, 2026
.Dt AS 1
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm as
.Nd Substrate assembler wrapper
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 32 | Fl 64
.Op Fl g
.Op Fl I Ar dir
.Op Fl D Ar macro
.Op Fl march Ar cpu
.Op Fl mtune Ar cpu
.Op Fl Wa Ar opts
.Op Fl -max-input-bytes Ar n
.Op Fl -max-line-bytes Ar n
.Op Fl -max-token-length Ar n
.Op Fl -max-macro-depth Ar n
.Op Fl -max-include-depth Ar n
.Op Fl o Ar output
.Ar input.s
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
invokes a backend compiler driver
.Pq usually
.Xr gcc 1
in assembler mode and validates the emitted object using
.Xr libelfobj 3 .
The wrapper selects 32-bit or 64-bit mode and performs ELF sanity checks.
.Pp
Optional hard limits can be set using
.Fl -max-input-bytes ,
.Fl -max-line-bytes ,
.Fl -max-token-length ,
.Fl -max-macro-depth ,
and
.Fl -max-include-depth .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width AS_BACKEND
.It Ev AS_BACKEND
Path/name of backend compiler driver executable. If unset,
.Nm
uses
.Ev CC
or falls back to
.Dq gcc .
.It Ev AS_ERROR_CODES
If set to a non-empty value,
.Nm
prefixes wrapper-originated diagnostics with a stable internal error code.
.It Ev AS_MAX_INPUT_BYTES
Default value for
.Fl -max-input-bytes .
.It Ev AS_MAX_LINE_BYTES
Default value for
.Fl -max-line-bytes .
.It Ev AS_MAX_TOKEN_LENGTH
Default value for
.Fl -max-token-length .
.It Ev AS_MAX_MACRO_DEPTH
Default value for
.Fl -max-macro-depth .
.It Ev AS_MAX_INCLUDE_DEPTH
Default value for
.Fl -max-include-depth .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ld 1 ,
.Xr cc 1
